//? Title: Latent Arithmetic: Explicit Paths Through a Frozen Decoder
//? Subtitle: Exact affine controls, fitting-label directions and unfiltered MNIST outputs
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Interpolating codes and adding a class-mean difference are explicit numerical operations.
This report applies them to a frozen 784–32–784 MNIST autoencoder, retaining every one of ten
fixed source/target pairs. A visible prerequisite reproduces the original three-epoch model;
the application makes zero new updates. Decoding a code interpolation differs from crossfading
decoded endpoints, with maximum pixel difference 0.179131. Class directions use fitting labels
and are compared with norm-matched random directions and pixel-mean edits. Negative edited
codes, clipping counts, ambiguous outputs and all failures are retained. No semantic-transport
or generative-prior claim follows from smooth probabilities.
)
\toc

> Choose a path, then decode its codes

An autoencoder separates an image-to-code encoder from a code-to-reconstruction decoder, as
described in [Goodfellow, Bengio and Courville, chapter 14](https://www.deeplearningbook.org/contents/autoencoders.html).
Here the encoder is ReLU and the decoder is an untied sigmoid layer. Its 32-coordinate bottleneck
is trained for reconstruction; an affine line through that space need not stay in a region
visited during fitting. This experiment examines explicit paths and controls for one small model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/latent_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(39, 1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle st;
  st.width     = 5.8;
  st.height    = 2.6;
  st.font_size = 18;
  d.node("x", {0, 4}, "Fixed held-out images\nFirst digit d / first digit d+1", st)
      .node("e", {8, 4}, "Frozen ReLU encoder\n784 -> 32", st)
      .node("p", {16, 4}, "Explicit code paths\nInterpolation / affine edits", st)
      .node("d", {24, 4}, "Frozen sigmoid decoder\nCodes only -> pixels", st)
      .edge("x", "e")
      .edge("e", "p")
      .edge("p", "d")
      .node("f", {8, -3}, "Fitting codes + labels\nPer-class code means", st)
      .node("v", {16, -3}, "Chosen direction\nNext mean - source mean", st)
      .edge("f", "v")
      .edge("v", "p")
      .text(
          {12, -8},
          "Class-mean edits use labels explicitly. Random directions match each code-space "
          "norm.\nAll 50,992 model values remain bit-exact; the application has no optimizer.",
          20)
      .save_svg("build/latent_method.svg");
}
```
