> A nonlinear decoder makes the distinction visible

For scalar endpoints a=-1 and b=1, z(t)=(1-t)a+tb=2t-1. Choose decoder
g(z)=[sigmoid(2z),sigmoid(-2z)]. At t=0.25, decoding z=-0.5 gives approximately
[0.269,0.731]; crossfading the decoded endpoints gives [0.310,0.690]. Both share the
endpoints, but the sigmoid curve and the pixel crossfade differ between them. At the midpoint,
symmetry makes both equal [0.5,0.5]. Smooth numbers alone do not certify a meaningful image.

For S=sum_t z(t), dS/da=sum_t(1-t), dS/db=sum_t t and dS/dt=b-a. These paths are
differentiated by the native API; no finite-difference substitute is used for the saved gradients.
The original two-products-then-sum grouping is retained, including Float32 rounding.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/latent_toy_decoder.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  namespace m     = n::models;
  const auto type = n::DType::Float64;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::ParameterStore p(7, type);
  const auto        a = n::full({1, 1}, -1, type), b = n::full({1, 1}, 1, type),
             alpha = n::linspace(0, 1, 21, type);
  m::UndercompleteDecoder(p, n::zeros({1, 1}, type), 2, 1);
  p.set("decoder/W", n::tensor({2., -2.}, {1, 2}, type));
  p.set("decoder/b", n::zeros({2}, type));
  const auto path    = m::LatentLerp(a, b, alpha),
             decoded = m::UndercompleteDecoder(p, m::LatentFlatten(path), 2, 1);
  const auto ea = m::UndercompleteDecoder(p, a, 2, 1), eb = m::UndercompleteDecoder(p, b, 2, 1);
  const auto crossfade = m::LatentFlatten(m::LatentLerp(ea, eb, alpha));
  std::print(
      "At t=.25: decoded {:.6f}; endpoint crossfade {:.6f}.\n",
      decoded.at({5, 0}),
      crossfade.at({5, 0}));
  auto aa = a.clone().requires_grad_(), bb = b.clone().requires_grad_(),
       tt      = n::tensor({0., .5, 1.}, {3}, type).requires_grad_();
  const auto g = n::grad(n::sum(m::LatentLerp(aa, bb, tt)), {aa, bb, tt});
  if (g[0].item() != 1.5 || g[1].item() != 1.5 ||
      g[2].to_vector<double>() != std::vector<double>(3, 2))
    return 1;
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(
          alpha.to_vector<double>(),
          n::select(decoded, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(),
          "Decode interpolated code",
          {37, 99, 235},
          2.)
      .lines(
          alpha.to_vector<double>(),
          n::select(crossfade, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(),
          "Crossfade decoded endpoints",
          {220, 38, 38},
          2.)
      .x_label("Interpolation level t")
      .y_label("First output probability")
      .title("A sigmoid decoder curves away from the pixel crossfade")
      .save_svg("build/latent_toy_decoder.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
At t=.25: decoded 0.268941; endpoint crossfade 0.309601.
\image(figures/latent_toy_decoder.svg)
// result_end
