> Interpolation: all ten pairs, with pixel crossfades beside the comparison

Rows correspond to source digits 0–9, with targets 1–9 then 0. Columns run from t=0 to t=1.
The first grid decodes the affine code path. Its endpoint columns reconstruct the selected
images; they are not claimed to equal the original pixels. The second grid crossfades those
original source/target pixels and is a baseline with a different geometry. Both grids keep every
pair, including blurred or ambiguous outputs. All five grids use the same fixed [0,1] display
scale, threefold integer enlargement and gray gaps.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/latent_latent_interpolations.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
