> Measure decoder curvature without naming semantic success

The maximum absolute difference between decoding interpolated codes and crossfading decoded
endpoints is 0.179131 over these pairs. The chart retains each pair's maximum difference across
all eleven levels and 784 pixels. This measures decoder nonlinearity for the selected paths,
not image quality or target-digit validity. Reverse code paths agree within 4.77e-7 because
Float32 interpolation levels are not exact decimal complements. Equal-code and zero-edit controls
also pass. There are 89 negative edited-code entries; they remain in the saved arrays and decoder
inputs. The pixel-mean control clips 8,587 entries and therefore answers a different question.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/latent_curvature.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> arrays;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz("build/latent/analysis.npz"))
    arrays.emplace(key, value);
  const auto difference = n::abs(
                              n::cast(arrays.at("interpolated_images"), n::DType::Float64) -
                              n::cast(arrays.at("decoder_endpoint_blends"), n::DType::Float64))
                              .reshape({10, 11, 784});
  const auto               values = n::max(difference, {1, 2}).to_vector<double>();
  std::vector<double>      digits;
  std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| source / target | maximum absolute decoder-crossfade difference |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit) {
    digits.push_back(digit);
    labels.push_back(std::to_string(digit) + "/" + std::to_string((digit + 1) % 10));
    std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n", labels.back(), values[digit]);
  }
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.bars(digits, values, "Maximum over levels and pixels", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, .65)
      .x_ticks(digits, labels)
      .x_label("Fixed source / target digit")
      .y_label("Maximum absolute probability difference")
      .title("Decoder curvature for every unfiltered pair")
      .save_svg("build/latent_curvature.svg");
}
```
