| 1/2 | 0.088947505 |
| 2/3 | 0.098381400 |
| 3/4 | 0.136967301 |
| 4/5 | 0.053636342 |
| 5/6 | 0.074868545 |
| 6/7 | 0.080890924 |
| 7/8 | 0.077909946 |
| 8/9 | 0.130503997 |
| 9/0 | 0.179130703 |
\image(figures/latent_curvature.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Every fixed pair has a measured discrepancy between its decoded code path and its decoded-endpoint crossfade. Neither path is evaluated for semantic success.)
\alttext(Ten bars giving maximum absolute decoder nonlinearity for the fixed zero-to-one through nine-to-zero digit pairs.)

> Scope and reproducibility

This is a posthoc analysis of one compact reconstruction model and one selected checkpoint.
It does not impose a learned prior, discover independent semantic factors or establish successful
class transport. Class directions explicitly use fitting labels, random directions provide a
matched-norm control, and all original cases remain visible. The visible prerequisite shows the
training cost; the frozen application changes no model values and makes zero new updates.

The optional independent NumPy oracle reads only the generated arrays. It verifies 13,760 affine
path values exactly, 8,160 class-centroid values, all 651 saved path derivatives, 320 Gaussian
values, both pixel controls, model immutability and 218,720 forward values. Maximum widened
forward error is below 5e-6. This check does not prepare data or fit the model.

> Reference

- Goodfellow, I., Bengio, Y. and Courville, A. (2016). *Deep Learning*, chapter 14,
  [Autoencoders](https://www.deeplearningbook.org/contents/autoencoders.html).
  The present ReLU/sigmoid architecture and affine edits are explicit teaching choices.
